{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>and behold, the nethek has spread in the skin — it is impure.</b> This verse is puzzling: why do I need it, when it is already said: 'והנה לא פשה הנתק וטהר אותו'? Perhaps one can say that were it not for this verse, I would have explained the verse 'והנה לא פשה הנתק' thus: if it did not spread and also there is no black hair in it — it is impure; but from spreading alone it would not become impure. Therefore Scripture says 'והנה פשה' — that from spreading alone it is impure."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:09.627334983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}